# SPA fallback for Cloudflare Pages and Netlify.
#
# This app routes in the browser, so /menu and /admin/orders exist only once
# React has loaded. A static host asked for them directly — a refresh, or a
# customer opening a shared link — looks for a file of that name, finds none,
# and serves its own 404. The site works until someone reloads, which is the
# worst possible way for it to break.
#
# 200, not 301: the URL must stay as the customer typed it so the router can
# read it. A redirect would rewrite the address bar to "/" and lose the page
# they asked for.
#
# Vercel does not read this file — it has the same rule in vercel.json.
/*    /index.html   200
